  "description": "The proposed development at 36 Craven Avenue includes the following modifications:\n1. Replacement of several UPVC windows with solid timber-framed windows, designed to match the proportions of some original windows found on the street.\n2. Removal and infill of one existing window and door, using brickwork to match the existing façade.\n3. Replacement of the current bi-fold door with a sliding door.\n4. Replacement of the existing garage door with a new timber door.\n5. Replacement of the front garden's timber fence with a combination of brick wall and timber fence.\n6. Replacement of the rear garden's timber fence with a brick wall.\n7. Erection of a small timber bin enclosure in the front garden.",
